"comparison": "Both Qualcomm and Intel disclose risks that their licensing activities or patent sales can lead to patent exhaustion, thereby limiting their ability to enforce IP rights against the buyers. Qualcomm specifically warns that selling chipsets to unlicensed OEMs could result in patent exhaustion claims that negate its ability to assert patents against those OEMs. Similarly, Intel notes that under current case law, patent licenses can exhaust Intel's patent rights regarding licensed product sales, and government or court decisions may require compulsory licensing or prevent enforcement, impairing IP value. Both companies identify exhaustion as a direct consequence of their licensing or sales strategies that negatively impacts their ability to monetize or enforce their IP portfolio.",
